From: =?UTF-8?q?Sven=20P=C3=BCschel?= <s.pueschel@pengutronix.de>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:24:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Make ENABLE_ZLIB_COMPRESSION an option
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

While other compression libraries have a dedicated option, the zlib
compression doesn't have an option and is unconditionally set to be
enabled. As already relevant conditional logic exists to disable zlib,
make it an option to allow the user to disable it.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/openSUSE/libsolv/pull/639]
Signed-off-by: Sven Püschel <s.pueschel@pengutronix.de>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 5ba5ed51b14b..62578f3554ff 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ OPTION (MULTI_SEMANTICS "Build with support for multiple distribution types?" OF
 
 OPTION (ENABLE_LZMA_COMPRESSION "Build with lzma/xz compression support?" OFF)
 OPTION (ENABLE_BZIP2_COMPRESSION "Build with bzip2 compression support?" OFF)
+OPTION (ENABLE_ZLIB_COMPRESSION "Build with zlib compression support?" ON)
 OPTION (ENABLE_ZSTD_COMPRESSION "Build with zstd compression support?" OFF)
 OPTION (ENABLE_ZCHUNK_COMPRESSION "Build with zchunk compression support?" OFF)
 OPTION (WITH_SYSTEM_ZCHUNK "Use system zchunk library?" OFF)
@@ -144,7 +145,6 @@ IF (${have_system} STRGREATER xx)
     MESSAGE (FATAL_ERROR "Can only compile for one system type.")
 ENDIF (${have_system} STRGREATER xx)
 
-SET (ENABLE_ZLIB_COMPRESSION ON)
 IF (ENABLE_ARCHREPO OR ENABLE_DEBIAN)
 SET (ENABLE_LZMA_COMPRESSION ON)
 ENDIF (ENABLE_ARCHREPO OR ENABLE_DEBIAN)
